Maintaining the Debian packaging of mmt-dpi
===========================================

debian/ lives in the upstream repository (montimage-projects/mmt-dpi). It
builds through `make -C sdk install-fhs` (FHS paths, upstream's SOVERSION) and is
independent of the upstream `make deb` package, which installs under /opt/mmt.

Binary packages
  libmmt-dpi1     libmmt_core.so.1 and the protocol plugins (tcpip, tmobile,
                  tdicom, business_app). The core dlopen()s the plugins from
                  /usr/lib/<triplet>/mmt-dpi/plugins/ (links to the libraries).
  libmmt-dpi-dev  headers (/usr/include/mmt-dpi), libmmt_*.so links,
                  mmt-dpi.pc, examples. Static archives are not shipped.
The security and fuzz engines (ENABLESEC=1, libxml2) are deliberately not
built for Debian yet.

Releasing a new upstream version
  1. Bump VERSION (docs/Prepare-for-a-new-released-version.md) and add a
     debian/changelog entry `<version>+ds-1`; scripts/validate-release-prep.sh
     (the version-agreement job and the tag's verify-tag job) fails otherwise.
  2. Tag vX.Y.Z. The release workflow attaches mmt-dpi-X.Y.Z.tar.gz
     (tools/ci/build-source-tarball.sh: `git archive` + `gzip -n`, byte
     reproducible), SHA256SUMS and a provenance attestation, and, once
     release signing is configured (below), mmt-dpi-X.Y.Z.tar.gz.asc.
  3. `uscan` finds that release asset through the GitHub releases API
     (debian/watch) — not GitHub's tag archive — and, because of
     Files-Excluded in debian/copyright, repacks it as
     mmt-dpi_X.Y.Z+ds.orig.tar.xz.
  4. Build in a clean chroot: `sbuild -d unstable` (or `pbuilder`), then run
     `lintian -i -I --pedantic` and `autopkgtest` on the result.

Changing the ABI
  SOVERSION is upstream's (end of rules/common.mk, issue #536; the abi-diff
  job fails an incompatible change that does not move it). When it moves,
  rename libmmt-dpi1 to libmmt-dpi<SOVERSION> in debian/control and the
  *.install / *.lintian-overrides file names.

Release signing (issue #538)
  The release job signs the source tarball with
  tools/ci/sign-source-tarball.sh. It needs two things only the maintainer
  can provide: the ASCII-armoured public release key committed as
  debian/upstream/signing-key.asc (with pgpsigurlmangle=s/$/.asc/ added to
  the opts of debian/watch in the same change), and the matching secret key
  in the repository secret MMT_RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY (plus
  MMT_RELEASE_SIGNING_PASSPHRASE when it has one). Until then releases ship
  unsigned with a warning; `sign-source-tarball.sh --check`
  (scripts/validate-release-prep.sh) fails a change that adds only one of
  the key and the watch option, and the release fails when the secret is
  missing or does not match the committed key.

CI
  The debian-package job of .github/workflows/release-packages.yml runs
  tools/ci/build-debian-package.sh on every Debian/Ubuntu distribution the
  release builds (Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04, 26.04, Debian 12, 13; amd64 and
  arm64). These .debs are checked, not published: the release assets and the
  bootstrap installer stay on the upstream `make deb` packages
  (docs/DECISIONS.md, issue #538).

Local check of the whole packaging
  docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/work -w /work debian:13 \
      bash tools/ci/build-debian-package.sh
  builds, lints, installs and runs the consumer against the installed files.

Blockers before an upload to Debian: see debian/license-audit.md and the
"Comment" of debian/copyright. The changelog still names a placeholder ITP
bug (#ITP-BUG-NUMBER) and the distribution is UNRELEASED.
